xmodel/as-fonly-residue-ball-collision-compactness-theorem-repaired-review-grok-20260825.md:45:**Correct, with one false parenthetical.** Fix finite allowed monomial sets \(S_P,S_Q\). Let \(X_n\subset\mathbb{Z}_3^N\) be coefficient vectors satisfying every coefficient of \(\det JF-1\) and the AS reduction modulo \(3^n\). Each \(X_n\) is closed. A solution over \(R_n\) lifts arbitrarily to \(\mathbb{Z}_3^N\), so \(X_n\) is nonempty whenever the finite scheme is. Nested nonempty compact sets have nonempty intersection; equivalently, the inverse system of nonempty finite solution sets has nonempty inverse limit (images in each \(S_n\) stabilize, then a thread exists). Exhibited solutions at different \(n\) need not be compatible.
