xmodel/keller-pencil-genus-review-grok46-20260902.md:266:**What “alone” is.** The only use of `Jac F ∈ C^*` in NVM’s intersection ledger is `R_aff=0`, which converts the general pairing into `NOETHER-K` `Z·K_X = −2N −κ + n(W−S)`. That identity does not bound `n(W−S)` or `Psi`. Combined with FORK-GENUS, `n(W−S) = 2N − Lambda + Psi`, so `NOETHER-K` rewrites the ceiling as a bound on fork mass and does not supply one. This is a theorem about this ledger.
