xmodel/websweep-0823.log:6479: | EC-K3-H3-Q8-QQ-D13 | Exact corrected H3 q8 neighbour over QQ with D13/MW4 child | On the exact H3 q6 E8+E6/MW3 child, the binary-quartic covariant is treated as a degree-two covering map, giving the primitive q8 marked section S=Pmap+Qmap with Mordell--Weil coordinate (-2,-2,0), height 24, zero intersection 10 and smooth collision divisor of degree ten. Clearing the full rational q-frame, including the Dx factor of x(S)=Nx/Dx, gives a 13-dimensional characteristic-zero Riemann--Roch ambient with eleven independent conditions and a two-dimensional pencil. Exact elimination produces a degree-four quartic whose Jacobian has one I9* fibre, nine I1 fibres and smooth infinity; hence its root lattice is D13 and its Mordell--Weil rank is four in Picard rank nineteen. This proves the second equation-level H3 neighbour E8+E6/MW3 -> D13/MW4. It does not construct the eleven later equation-level neighbours to the rootless MW17 frame or identify curve 273 as a specialization. | [source](elkies-k3/H3_Q8_REAUDIT_2026-08-22.md) | `EC-K3-H3-Q6`, `EC-K3-H3-Q8-CHILD-MARKING` | [checker](elkies-k3/scripts/derive_h92_q6_child_q8_corrected2cover_qq.sage) | exact_symbolic; `sha256:01da6b84ee1f…`; locks: `elkies-k3/data/fibrations/h3_q8_component_nef_physical_root_target.json`, `elkies-k3/scripts/derive_h92_q6_child_q8_corrected2cover_qq.sage`; updates: narrows problems `OP-EC-NEXT` | — |
