The stronger `V_s/u_s - 1` principal floor kills 33 groups, but §7.3 does not make that exact for `u_s>1` without additional split data. I’m switching the promoted driver to the weaker fail-closed policy: use the exact principal contribution only when `u_s=1`; use `0` for `u_s>1`. This still leaves a genuine `u_s>1` signal, just not one resting on an unproved principal split assumption.
